meta {
  name: Set Availability
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/availability
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "is_available": false
  }
}

docs {
  # Set Master Availability

  The master's own on/off switch for work. While `is_available` is `false` the
  administrator cannot assign them to an order (the attempt returns 422) and
  the auto-search skips them.

  Blocking a master or letting their subscription lapse flips this to `false`
  automatically — it is not left dangling as `true`.

  **Body:**
  | Field          | Type    | Required | Description                            |
  |----------------|---------|----------|----------------------------------------|
  | `is_available` | boolean | yes      | `true` = ready for work, `false` = not |

  **Response 200:** `MasterProfileResource`

  **Errors:**
  - `401` — missing / invalid token
  - `403` — token has no usable master profile (see `reason`)
  - `422` — `is_available` missing or not boolean
}
